 {id:'academy',chapter:'Big moves',layout:'image',image:'academy',label:'Frontline learning',title:'A classroom.\nThen a real car.',body:'Bangalore’s first Cars24 Training Academy opened in Jakkur on 26ᵗʰ October. Frontline teams begin with classroom refreshers, then put the learning to work on real cars. The first sessions started with CJ refreshers.',credit:'Sejal Sanjay Sangole · #builders-cars24',note:'Illustration created for The Pitstop. An imagined academy scene, not a photograph of the opening.'},
 {id:'growth',chapter:'Big moves',layout:'stat',label:'H1 FY27',stat:'₹5,300',unit:'crore+ in gross merchandise value',title:'More business.\nStronger economics.',body:'Gross merchandise value grew about 29% year on year. Adjusted net revenue reached ₹921 crore, up more than 33%. The EBITDA loss narrowed to around 1% of gross merchandise value.',credit:'Aditya Mittal · Company-wide H1 FY27 update',note:'Gross merchandise value is the total value of transactions. EBITDA is a measure of operating earnings. Figures are as reported in the supplied edition.'},
 {id:'ecosystem',chapter:'Big moves',layout:'stat',label:'Across the business',stat:'4×',unit:'year-on-year margin growth',title:'The wider ecosystem\nis growing too.',body:'Ecosystem services and insurance generated ₹160 crore+ in margin. Consumer deliveries grew about 68% in H1. In September, UAE and Australia each crossed roughly 700 cars in a month for the first time.',credit:'Aditya Mittal · Company-wide H1 FY27 update'},
 {id:'frontier',chapter:'Big moves',layout:'image',image:'frontier',label:'Coming up · 29ᵗʰ November',title:'30+ AI releases.\nOne day in Delhi.',body:'At Frontier ’26, Cars24 and Deployment Inc plan to unveil more than 30 AI releases. VC’s announcement also promises a look at the work of rebuilding an enterprise around AI.',credit:'VC · #announcements · 28ᵗʰ October',note:'Future event, as announced in the October edition. Artwork is an imagined editorial illustration.'},
 {id:'startup',chapter:'Big moves',layout:'statement',label:'Grand Startup Challenge',title:'Big problems.\nEarly builders.',accent:'₹1 crore prize pool',body:'Cars24 is inviting early-stage teams working on fintech, road safety, supply chains, and sovereign AI. The top 20 receive a month of mentorship in December, before a New Delhi finale in January 2027.',foot:'Apply by 10ᵗʰ November, 11:59 p.m. IST',link:'https://gsc.cars24.com',linkLabel:'Explore the challenge',credit:'Yuvika Sharma · #announcements / #builders-cars24 · 29ᵗʰ October',note:'Partners: Startup India (DPIIT), MeitY Startup Hub, and Startup Policy Forum. The four tracks are Lending & Fintech, Mobility & Road Safety, Logistics & Supply Chain, and Sovereign AI.'},
 {id:'lending',chapter:'Big moves',layout:'stat',label:'Loans24 · Festive milestone',stat:'₹22',unit:'crore disbursed in one day',title:'A record day\nfor lending.',body:'C2C and Loans24 recorded 414 disbursals in a single day. Volume was twice last Navratri’s first day. Internal attach reached 50%, with overall attach at 53.7%.',credit:'Ujjwal Mehrotra · #loans24 · 12ᵗʰ October',note:'The supplied lending update also reports 771 deliveries, while the customer story reports 770 handovers. That conflicting delivery figure is omitted here pending reconciliation. Attach percentages are retained as reported.'},
 {id:'handovers',chapter:'People & places',layout:'image',image:'customer',label:'Customer love',title:'770 handovers.\nOne at 3 a.m.',body:'On Navratri’s first day, 770 customers drove home in a car. In Dombivli, a delivery coordinator and car advisor stayed until 3 a.m. for an auspicious handover. They were back at the hub the next morning.',credit:'Piyush Narula · #announcements · 11ᵗʰ October',note:'Teams across Wholesale, Experience, RTO, Operations, and Finance contributed. Artwork is an imagined handover scene.'},
 {id:'waits',chapter:'People & places',layout:'statement',label:'The next improvement',title:'A great day\ncan get better.',accent:'Less waiting at the hub.',body:'The record handover day brought longer waits at some hubs. Piyush called it out in the same update. As more customers arrive, the next job is to make the experience smoother for every one of them.',credit:'Piyush Narula · #announcements · 11ᵗʰ October'},
 {id:'dehradun',chapter:'People & places',layout:'image',image:'business',label:'A new home in Dehradun',title:'A first hub.\nA familiar kind of pride.',body:'Dehradun’s first Cars24 Hub opened on 25ᵗʰ October. The launch brought frontline champions and their families together. A top-performing Wholesale Sales Manager inaugurated the hub.',credit:'Sumit Kumar · Hub launch update',note:'The image illustrates a Cars24 hub; it does not depict the Dehradun opening.'},
 {id:'pdi',chapter:'People & places',layout:'image',image:'akbar-birbal',label:'A story worth a closer look',title:'Akbar, Birbal,\nand a car inspection.',body:'Cars24’s first Pre-Delivery Inspection brand film borrows a familiar Akbar–Birbal tale. Anmol Sharma shared the story, with a simple message: give every ride a closer look before it heads out on the road.',credit:'Anmol Sharma · Brand film update',note:'Created with Pushkal Arora, Vedika Gulati, Akriti Kohli, Vipul Setia, Prachi S, Manuj Chawla, and Sakshi Agarwal. Artwork painted for The Pitstop; not a film still.'},
 {id:'telugu',chapter:'People & places',layout:'image',image:'telugu',label:'Made for Telugu audiences',title:'A familiar star.\nA local voice.',body:'Vipul Setia shared a collaboration byte from Cars24’s first Telugu Meta creative, featuring Vijay Deverakonda. It brings the car-buying story to audiences in their own language.',credit:'Vipul Setia · Telugu creative update',note:'Imagined editorial illustration of Vijay Deverakonda. This is not a campaign still or evidence of an endorsement beyond the supplied announcement.'},
 {id:'dealer',chapter:'Freshly shipped',layout:'statement',label:'Dealer App · Rishabh',title:'Offer terms,\nwithout the detour.',accent:'Create them in the app.',body:'Dealers can now customise and generate offer terms directly in the Dealer App. The existing approval process stays in place. The change is expected to reduce the time between an offer and its terms.',credit:'Rishabh · Product release update'},
 {id:'miles',chapter:'Freshly shipped',layout:'stat',label:'Miles · Rishabh and team',stat:'+15%',unit:'monthly visits targeted',title:'More field visits\ncan make it in.',body:'Field teams can now record unplanned visits with new dealers and loan customers in Miles. The release targets 15% more monthly visits and 10% more leads entering the system.',credit:'Rishabh and team · Miles release update',note:'These are release targets, not measured outcomes.'},
 {id:'leads',chapter:'Freshly shipped',layout:'statement',label:'C2C · Diya Mariya Manoj and team',title:'Call the people\nwho are ready.',accent:'A clearer lead queue.',body:'The refreshed queue gives more priority to customers who show interest through AIRO handoffs or calls. Booking progress helps organise the next tiers, giving teams a clearer order for following up.',credit:'Diya Mariya Manoj and team · C2C release update'},
 {id:'approvals',chapter:'Freshly shipped',layout:'statement',label:'C2C · Diya Mariya Manoj and team',title:'Less chasing.\nMore knowing.',accent:'Approval status, in view.',body:'Sales teams can now see whether a partner approval is pending, in progress, or complete in the C2C panel. That means fewer messages asking where an approval stands.',credit:'Diya Mariya Manoj and team · C2C release update'},
 {id:'saarathi',chapter:'Freshly shipped',layout:'statement',label:'Saarathi · Monu Goyal and team',title:'Keep the offer\nconversation moving.',accent:'More tools at the yard.',body:'Ground agents can adjust offer details and down payments, check offer history, and generate terms for eligible system offers. The tools help them work through the next step with the customer, right there at the yard.',credit:'Monu Goyal and team · Saarathi release update',note:'The source calls the adjustable field “ROI”. Its expansion is not established in the source, so the short copy uses “offer details”.'},
 {id:'ownership',chapter:'Freshly shipped',layout:'statement',label:'Deemed Ownership',title:'The backend\nis live.',accent:'App checks come next.',body:'All Deemed Ownership backend systems reached production on 28ᵗʰ October. Teams were completing production and app checks. The app release was targeted for 29ᵗʰ October, subject to those checks.',credit:'Hemant Garg and teams · 28ᵗʰ October',note:'The supplied edition does not confirm the app shipped. This card preserves the status at the edition’s reporting cut-off.'},
 {id:'security',chapter:'Freshly shipped',layout:'statement',label:'Technology watch',title:'A patch\nthat needs priority.',accent:'Update. Redeploy. Confirm.',body:'A dependency security advisory is being handled as a priority patch-and-redeploy effort. Affected service owners have been asked to confirm when their work is complete.',credit:'Technology security advisory · Supplied October edition',note:'The source does not identify the dependency or provide an advisory link. Do not treat this card as a substitute for the technical advisory.'},
 {id:'codex',chapter:'How we work',layout:'image',image:'team',label:'Builders at work',title:'From Figma\nto a usable draft.',body:'Ishaan Kothiyal tested a Codex + Figma workflow that produced a V3 homepage draft in the CMS. Early estimated effort savings: 20–30%. Production readiness still needs validation. Next up: testing it across 23 SEO pages.',credit:'Ishaan Kothiyal · Workflow update',note:'Also credited: Nitin Sharma, Premveer Tomar, Sumit Sharma, and Mayank. Savings are an early estimate. The artwork is an imagined team scene.'},
 {id:'hackathon',chapter:'How we work',layout:'stat',label:'People & Culture Hackathon',stat:'48',unit:'hours of building',title:'Everyday admin.\nFresh approaches.',body:'Teams tackled payroll inputs, compliance tracking, recurring WeCare tickets, and a Manager Hub. The update reported automation progress reaching 36%. A proposed workflow aims to cut WeCare tickets by 40%.',credit:'Gaurav Saxena · Outcomes highlighted by Shivanshu Makkar',note:'Contributors included Aayush Gupta, Divyansh Bansal, Nikhil Meena, Shreeya Arora, Manvi Mehrotra, Shloka Patnaik, Shobhan Suri, Gaurav Saxena, and Vivek Naiwal. Teams also rethought induction and built a shared hub for SOPs, agents, and data. The 40% reduction is a proposed target, not a result.'},
 {id:'milo',chapter:'How we work',layout:'statement',label:'Wellbeing · Rashi Bajaj',title:'A place\nto check in.',accent:'Meet Milo on Slack.',body:'Rashi Bajaj introduced Milo, a confidential AI wellbeing companion on Slack. It offers another way to check in with yourself. It is not a replacement for therapy.',credit:'Rashi Bajaj · Milo introduction',note:'Confidentiality is described as stated in the supplied announcement. No independent privacy or clinical assessment was performed.'},
 {id:'badminton',chapter:'How we work',layout:'statement',label:'Badminton championship',title:'Good work.\nGreat rallies.',accent:'A round of applause.',body:'Goldarin Kumar and Harshita Khajuria won singles and mixed doubles. Kunal Singla and Vasu Chauhan won men’s doubles. Aditya Ghai received the Spirit of the Games award.',credit:'Arjun Lal · Championship results'},
 {id:'survey',chapter:'How we work',layout:'statement',label:'Voice of Autonauts',title:'Tell us\nhow it’s going.',accent:'The survey is in Darwinbox.',body:'A fresh Voice of Autonauts survey is live. Earlier feedback has informed work on incentive clarity, WeCare tickets, IT infrastructure, and hub hygiene. Your everyday experience is useful feedback.',credit:'People & culture · Supplied October edition',note:'Survey availability reflects the supplied edition; no current live survey URL was supplied.'},
 {id:'finance',chapter:'How we work',layout:'statement',label:'Australia Finance',title:'Find the gaps.\nFix the process.',accent:'The War Room has begun.',body:'The Australia Finance team has started reviewing its processes from end to end. The aim is to surface pain points and gaps, then build a roadmap to address them.',credit:'Nishant Arora · Australia Finance update'},
 {id:'close',chapter:'How we work',layout:'statement',label:'Finance · Operating rhythm',title:'A clearer view\nof the numbers.',accent:'Repeatable work, done better.',body:'Across Finance, Raghav Khanna and Shivanshu Makkar highlighted the September close, clearer city and region reporting, and repeatable process automation.',credit:'Raghav Khanna and Shivanshu Makkar · Finance updates'},
 {id:'ambition',chapter:'Take it with you',layout:'image',image:'perspective',label:'A thought from VC',title:'Choose something\nworth attempting.',body:'Ahead of Frontier ’26, VC’s note was to meet this AI moment with ambition: pick problems worth trying to solve, and build things that change what people think is possible.',credit:'VC · Frontier ’26 announcement · 28ᵗʰ October',note:'Paraphrased from the supplied edition; not a direct quotation. Artwork is an imagined editorial scene.'},
 {id:'controls',chapter:'Take it with you',layout:'statement',label:'A thought from Shivanshu Makkar',title:'Let clear rules\ndo routine checks.',accent:'Save people for the exceptions.',body:'When a rule is clear, the system can check routine cases continuously. People can then focus on the exceptions, instead of making every request wait for manual approval.',credit:'Shivanshu Makkar · #builders-cars24 · 23ʳᵈ October',note:'Paraphrase, not a direct quotation.'},
 {id:'inflection',chapter:'Take it with you',layout:'statement',label:'A thought from Ruchit',title:'Big shifts take\nmany teams.',accent:'The pieces landed together.',body:'When the Deemed Ownership backend reached production, Ruchit called it the start of a paradigm shift. It was a shared milestone, with app checks still ahead.',credit:'Ruchit · #24-hrs-rct-deemed-ownership · 28ᵗʰ October',note:'Paraphrase, not a direct quotation. Backend launch and app release are separate milestones.'},
 {id:'safeguards',chapter:'Take it with you',layout:'statement',label:'A thought from Himanshu Rathore',title:'As products grow,\nsafeguards must too.',accent:'Security grows with the work.',body:'Data, infrastructure, and code security need to keep pace with the product, especially when customer and payment information is involved.',credit:'Himanshu Rathore · #cfi-product-tech · 27ᵗʰ October',note:'Paraphrase, not a direct quotation.'},
 {id:'thermostat',chapter:'One last thing',layout:'winter',label:'The office weather report',title:'The thermostat\nis still negotiating.',accent:'SAS Tower · Winter arc',body:'It’s taking more feedback than a product launch. It still hasn’t found a setting everyone likes.',credit:'The Pitstop · October’s lighter moment'}
